,"received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #6017\n\n## What\n\nDated design record settling issue #6017 (worlds design programme #5955): the capability observability surface, specified against the #5958 registry schema (consumed verbatim from the design record in PR #7599 — field names are references, not re-definitions).\n\n- **Audience×surface matrix**: users / world authors / server admins × the surfaces each actually gets, with the exact records each view reads.\n- **User views**: granted set from `effective_grant` (annotated by `requested`), used set rendered state-first from `discovered_used` (unknown ≠ empty — an uncertified world never renders as \"uses nothing\"), `observed` kept as a separate weaker post-connect line; changed-since-last-connection populated from the history log.\n- **Author views**: requested-vs-used diffs, inherited library footprint decomposed by release-identity closure member, uncertified-derivation markings (state + `partial` under its `non_authoritative` label; policy stays #6000's).\n- **Admin views**: grants in force (`effective_grant` + `custom_platform`), per-server capability inventory, moderation-pack provenance tuple (pack id, version, feeds, applied_at) with the moderation-sibling dependency named explicitly.\n- **History (§5)**: append-only capability event log keyed by `(world_id, release_identity)` with field-level diffs — the layer #5958 §4.3 explicitly deferred to #6017 — plus the three queries it must answer. `observed` deliberately excluded (rolling window, not history).\n- **Sibling coordination table**: #5958/PR #7599 dependency named (record open at writing), #5960 merged, #5959/#5961/#6000/#5840 boundaries stated; no silent assumptions.\n\nDocs only: one new design record + one planning/architecture/README.md index line. No code change.\n\nQueue task 13008, lane code-m.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796726058&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7640&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7640&signature=251fedd997ce555917d253a7c6a1c709901e6c94a6366db044c33264355a4cb1\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7640?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-08T10:34:15Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T10:34:42Z","closed_at":"2026-11-08T10:34:39Z","merged_at":"2026-11-08T10:34:39Z","merge_commit_sha":"e6818e17a3daed99de5630340eb1d03781068ed8","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com